<title>UK: ISO details revised 1996/97 sugar output forecasts.</title>
<headline>ISO details revised 1996/97 sugar output forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table of output estimates for the world's major sugar producers, as forecast by the International Sugar Organization (ISO) in its second revision issued late on Friday.</p>
<p>Figures are in millions of tonnes, raw value.</p>
<p>COUNTRY		   1996/97		  1995/96</p>
<p>Australia		   5.70		     5.35</p>
<p>Brazil		     13.50		    14.63</p>
<p>China			 7.10		     6.79</p>
<p>Cuba			  4.80		     4.64</p>
<p>European Union	   18.00		    16.95</p>
<p>India			15.50		    17.67</p>
<p>Russia			1.90		     2.18</p>
<p>Thailand		    6.50		     6.38</p>
<p>Ukraine		     2.98		     3.90</p>
<p>WORLD TOTAL	     123.34		   123.90</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
